<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_66f14f762d9ed93be7e45532f52e341584cfa69a96a4b48ae6ab5277a1a358e7_n0035/e_0011> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/PatientCondition> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_66f14f762d9ed93be7e45532f52e341584cfa69a96a4b48ae6ab5277a1a358e7_n0035/e_0033/normalization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/EntityNormalization> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_66f14f762d9ed93be7e45532f52e341584cfa69a96a4b48ae6ab5277a1a358e7_n0035/tu_0003> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "Ivabradine should be considered in symptomatic patients with LVEF ≤35%, in SR and a resting heart rate ≥70 b.p.m. despite treatment with an evidence-based dose of beta-blocker (or maximum tolerated dose below that), ACE-I/(or ARNI), and an MRA, to reduce the risk of HF hospitalization and CV death. 139" .
