<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_66f14f762d9ed93be7e45532f52e341584cfa69a96a4b48ae6ab5277a1a358e7_n0035/e_0048> <http://digistrucmed.org/spanConfidence> "1.0"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_66f14f762d9ed93be7e45532f52e341584cfa69a96a4b48ae6ab5277a1a358e7_n0035/tu_0004> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "Ivabradine should be considered in symptomatic patients with LVEF ≤35%, in SR and a resting heart rate ≥70 b.p.m. who are unable to tolerate or have contraindications for a beta-blocker to reduce the risk of HF hospitalization and CV death. Patients should also receive an ACE-I (or ARNI) and an MRA. 140" .
